# Repository-root build context.
#
# The G5 gate builds docker/hydraulic-gates/g5-browser.Dockerfile with this
# directory as the context, so this is the only .dockerignore it reads (the
# compose builds use contexts ./backend and ./frontend and keep their own
# ignore rules, untouched here). Without it every G5 build uploads the whole
# working tree: backend/.venv alone is 1.7 GiB and frontend/node_modules
# another 377 MiB, none of which the G5 image consumes.
#
# Every entry is a pattern, never a bare top-level directory, so none of them
# can narrow a ./backend or ./frontend context for another build. Nothing the
# G5 image needs is excluded: frontend/package.json, frontend/package-lock.json,
# frontend/.npmrc, frontend/src, frontend/public, frontend/performance and the
# frontend build config all stay in context.
#
# This takes the context from 2.4 GiB to roughly 200 MiB.

.git
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.tsbuildinfo
artifacts
**/*.db
**/*.log
.env
.env.*
